    "question": "Sheik, I sit on a chair to do my sajda because of my healt condition. But in masjid I have to keep the chair in front by a foot in front of others in masjid , if I put it on the line so many men argue with me to put my chair in front so I cannot argue back as everyone else listens to them and they are elders as well. So what should I do?",
    "content": "You should stand with the row and once you want to sit down, you should take one step forward and pull the chair with you so that you now also sit with the row. The easiest way is that when you go to the sujood position, you take one step forward while pulling the chair with you. This will leave the whole row for the one behind you to prostrate normally. Once you stand up, you push the chair backwards and stand inline.",
