    "question": "I suffer from cervical ectropion from 4 years and have abnormal vaginal discharge ever since. It is getting very difficult to wash my private parts before every salah. Excessive washing is making the vaginal health worse and washing so often caused severe contact dermatitis on hands. Can I combine prayers? And is it sufficient to run water over the private area instead of washing to attain purity?",
    "content": "If these are your normal vaginal discharges, you don’t need to wash them off to pray nor to perform wudhu as these are not najis. If these are other than your vaginal discharges such as the result of infection, this is najis and requires that you only wash the affected area once the athan is called and make wudhu and pray. You don’t need to wash it off except before praying and not every time it is discharged.",
    "excerpt": "If these are your normal vaginal discharges, you don’t need to wash them off to pray nor to perform wudhu as these are not najis. If these are other than your vaginal discharges such as the result of infection, this is najis and requires that you only wash the affected area once the athan [&hellip;]",
